103: ### 1.3 Latent Defect: `replaceAll` Replacement Pattern Dollar Sign (`$`) Corruption
104: - In `restoreFn`:
105:   ```ts
106:   restored = restored.replaceAll(placeholder, original);
107:   ```
108: - If `original` contains `$` followed by digits or special characters (e.g. `sk-test$1$2$$` or `sk-$&`):
109:   - In JavaScript, `String.prototype.replaceAll(str, replacementString)` interprets `$&` (matched placeholder), `$'` (following string), `$\`` (preceding string), and `$$` (`$`).
110:   - Running `"Here is [API_KEY_1]".replaceAll("[API_KEY_1]", "sk-$&")` produces `"Here is sk-[API_KEY_1]"` instead of `"Here is sk-$&"`.
111:   - Using a replacer function `restored.replaceAll(placeholder, () => original)` treats `original` strictly as a literal string, completely eliminating `$` corruption.
112: 
